  "translation": "Today our whole family went to the East Gate Market together. The fruit there is very fresh, and the prices are also very cheap. Mom bought two cups of juice, and Dad picked several apples. I saw that the stalls had many vegetables, all grown by the farmers themselves. My sister saw an old man selling fresh flowers, and she immediately ran over. I asked her: 'What do you want to buy?' She said: 'I want to buy a bunch of flowers and give them to Mom.' I thought this idea was really good. Later, we also bought some seafood and prepared to cook a big dinner in the evening. The market was very lively inside. I asked my dad: 'Can you cook seafood?' Dad smiled and said: 'Of course I can!' I was very happy because today we can eat a delicious dinner. The sun set in the west, and we carried big and small bags home. It was really a pleasant weekend!"
